const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"分数越高，股东权利越弱",en:"Check the direction before reading the score"},body:{zh:"论文汇总24项治理条款，形成衡量股东权利的指数。数值较高代表对股东权利的限制更多，而不是“治理更好”。这也不是环境、社会与治理的综合评分。解释任何分组或图表之前，先确认计分方向及条款到底衡量谁的权利。",en:"The index combines 24 governance provisions: a higher score indicates weaker shareholder rights, not better governance. It is also not a combined environmental, social and governance rating. Before interpreting a group comparison or chart, establish the coding direction and whose rights the underlying provisions describe."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w8449/w8449.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2001年8月NBER工作论文，第1–3, 7–8页",en:"Source: August 2001 NBER working paper, pp. 1–3, 7–8"}}},{title:{zh:"覆盖范围决定结论的边界",en:"Coverage defines the comparison"},body:{zh:"工作论文使用约1500家大型公司的治理资料，研究时期为1990至1999年，并排除双重股权结构公司。资料覆盖在后期发生扩展。因此样本不是所有上市公司的固定全集，跨期比较需要区分治理变化与被纳入资料库的公司变化。",en:"The working paper uses governance information for roughly 1,500 large companies over 1990–1999 and excludes dual-class firms. Coverage expands later in the period. This is not a fixed census of all listed companies; a time comparison must distinguish changing provisions from changes in which firms enter the source database."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w8449/w8449.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2001年8月NBER工作论文，第2, 7–8页",en:"Source: August 2001 NBER working paper, pp. 2, 7–8"}}},{title:{zh:"州法存在，不代表每家公司都适用",en:"State law does not establish firm-level coverage"},body:{zh:"作者在公司文件之外补充州反收购法，并按公司注册地及退出适用安排编码。如果公司已选择退出某项法律，研究将其视为该法不适用。因此不能仅凭注册州就赋同一个分数；章程、细则与当时生效的选择需要一起核对。这描述的是历史研究编码，不是当前法律意见。",en:"The authors supplement company documents with state takeover laws, considering incorporation and firm-level opt-out choices. A firm opting out is coded as not covered by that law. State of incorporation alone therefore cannot assign an identical score to every firm; dated charter and bylaw choices matter. This describes historical research coding, not current legal advice."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w8449/w8449.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2001年8月NBER工作论文，第9–10页",en:"Source: August 2001 NBER working paper, pp. 9–10"}}},{title:{zh:"资料版本不是实时状态",en:"A publication vintage is not a live state"},body:{zh:"治理资料来自1990、1993、1995和1998年的多个版本，并非每次都会更新所有公司的全部条款。相邻版本数值相同，不足以证明期间没有变化。与行情连接时还要校验公司标识和样本匹配，不能把最新一版指数直接回填到过去。",en:"Governance observations come from the 1990, 1993, 1995 and 1998 publications, without a complete refresh of every company at each edition. An unchanged value does not prove that nothing changed between observations. Matching market data requires validated firm identities and dated vintages, not backfilling history with the latest index."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w8449/w8449.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2001年8月NBER工作论文，第7–8页",en:"Source: August 2001 NBER working paper, pp. 7–8"}}},{title:{zh:"同为一分，不代表影响相同",en:"Equal points do not imply equal effects"},body:{zh:"指数采用二元、等权计分，不区分同一条款的强弱，也不声称一分对应相同财富影响。秘密投票和累积投票是方向例外：它们增强股东权利，缺少时才加一分。把所有条款机械地按“存在就加分”汇总，会颠倒这两项含义；原始条款与编码规则都应保留。",en:"Binary, equal-weight coding does not distinguish provision strength or assign an equal wealth effect to each point. Secret ballots and cumulative voting are exceptions: a point is added when they are absent because their presence strengthens shareholder rights. Summing every provision as present-equals-one reverses these two meanings; retain both the raw provision and its coding rule."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w8449/w8449.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2001年8月NBER工作论文，第9, 11–12页",en:"Source: August 2001 NBER working paper, pp. 9, 11–12"}}},{title:{zh:"相关性留下了因果问题",en:"Association leaves causality unresolved"},body:{zh:"作者明确不把这些关系当作因果方向已经确定的证明。治理条款可能影响经营，也可能在公司预期表现恶化时被采用，或者只是其他问题的伴随特征。若想评价一次治理改革，需要额外识别设计，而不是把历史组间差异直接解释为改革收益。",en:"The authors explicitly refrain from claiming a settled direction of causality. Provisions might affect operations, be adopted in anticipation of poor performance or indicate other underlying problems. Evaluating a governance reform requires an additional identification design; a historical difference between groups is not itself the return to implementing that reform."},reference:{url:"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w8449/w8449.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2001年8月NBER工作论文，第4–6页",en:"Source: August 2001 NBER working paper, pp. 4–6"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"导读依据2001年工作论文，题录保留2003年期刊版。历史美国治理条款不能直接视为当前法律或跨市场治理标准；相关关系不等于治理改革的因果效果。",en:"This guide uses the 2001 working paper while retaining the 2003 journal citation. Historical US provisions are not current law or a cross-market governance standard; associations do not identify the causal effect of governance reform."}};export{e as default};
